# Level 2-06: Grand Convergence — the World 2 capstone. Reuses 2-01/2-04's exact two-ghost/
# two-plate AND-door spine unchanged (plate a left at row 4, plate b right at row 9, AND-door
# at row 13), then chains 2-05's platform gap directly onto 2-04's box-and-turn ending, all in
# one final approach: cross the platform, then push the box, then reach the goal. Branch to
# plate a: (5,4)-(4,4)-(3,4)-(2,4)-(1,4). Branch to plate b: (5,9)-(6,9)-(7,9)-(8,9)-(9,9). Past
# the door at (5,13): platform waypoints P (5,14, order 0) and Q (5,16, order 1) straddle a
# solid one-tile chasm at (5,15) — same deliberate, hand-verified "no walked path needed between
# named waypoints" exception used by 2-03/2-05/4-03. From Q, the box at (5,17) blocks the spine;
# pushing it up into the dead-end catch stub at (5,18) clears (5,17) for a turn right into
# (6,17)-(7,17)=goal, exactly like 2-04/3-04's box-and-turn ending. Every tile is a single-width
# extension of the spine or one of its branches/stubs, connected back to spawn (5,0); nothing is
# enclosed by more than one connection.
#
# Convoy note (full derivation in 2-01/MoveResolver.cs): every actor resets to the identical
# spawn tile every loop, so whichever actor departs later idles one extra tick per
# already-in-motion actor before its first step, then follows exactly one tile behind. The
# two-ghost section below is identical to 2-01/2-04, so only the results are restated.
#
# Loop 0 (ghost1 recording, alone): t0-3 Up x4 to (5,4). t4-7 Left x4 to (1,4)=plate a, active
#   end of t7. Loop runs its timer; ghost1 spawns, holding a forever after.
# Loop 1 (ghost2 recording, ghost1 replaying): player idles t0 (1 tick), departs t1. Ticks1-9
#   Up x9 to (5,9) [passes the plate-a junction at t4 without turning]. Ticks10-13 Right x4 to
#   (9,9)=plate b, active end of t13. Loop runs its timer; ghost2 spawns, holding b forever
#   after.
# Loop 2 (final — both ghosts replaying unperturbed, live player unencumbered plus platform
#   and box):
#   Player idles t0-1 (2 ticks), departs t2, staying a constant 1-tile gap behind ghost2
#   (itself 1 tile behind ghost1).
#   Ticks2-14: Up x13, reaching the door tile (5,13) on tick14. Plate a held since t7, plate b
#     since t13 — both well before t14 — so the AND door is already open, no bump.
#   Tick15: Up (5,13)->(5,14)=P. ticksPerStep=6 for this platform: WaypointAt(t)=waypoints[
#     floor(t/6)%2]. floor(14/6)=2 (even) -> P, floor(15/6)=2 (even) -> P still — the platform
#     is simply sitting there when the player steps on, no surprise transition.
#   Ticks16-17: Idle, idle (still inside the P window: floor(16/6)=2, floor(17/6)=2, both -> P).
#   Tick18: Idle — the transition tick. WaypointAt(17)=P, WaypointAt(18)=floor(18/6)=3 (odd)
#     -> Q. The player, having idled through t16-t18, still has a post-move position of P at the
#     end of t18 — matching the platform's pre-tick position — so the carry rule relocates them
#     with it: (5,14)->(5,16).
#   Tick19: Up: target (5,17) where the box sits. Far side (5,18) is the plain, empty catch
#     stub — push is legal: box (5,17)->(5,18), player -> (5,17). Turn row now clear.
#   Tick20: Right (5,17)->(6,17). Tick21: Right (6,17)->(7,17)=goal. WinCondition satisfied at
#     tick 21.
# Totals: 3 loops used (2 ghost loops + 1 final) -> PAR_LOOPS: 3 (matches MAX_TIMELINES: 2 fully
#   used, i.e. two ghosts plus the final live pass).
#   21 ticks in the winning loop -> PAR_TICKS: 28 (generous buffer, matching World 2's
#   not-a-precision-challenge style throughout).
NAME: 2-06 Grand Convergence
WORLD: 2
LOOP_SECONDS: 24
MAX_TIMELINES: 2
PAR_LOOPS: 3
PAR_TICKS: 28
GRID:
